1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Every morning, a restaurant must decide what to prep,
what will run short, and what to order before service.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Kitchen Prep Taskmaster completes that whole job automatically,
and shows its work.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:23,000
At seven, Cloud Scheduler securely triggers a private Cloud Run worker.
No chat and no button click.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:32,000
The agent combines bookings, weather, sales history,
recipes, and batch inventory.

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Gemini proposes demand. Python validates, applies FEFO,
calculates shortfalls and orders, and publishes to Firestore.

6
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Gemini has exactly two bounded jobs:
propose dish demand and write the briefing.

7
00:00:51,000 --> 00:01:00,000
It never owns an ingredient, inventory, shortfall,
order, or delivery quantity.

8
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Every proposal is validated. If it fails, a deterministic baseline
takes over and the dashboard visibly marks the degraded path.

9
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:19,000
The mutation surface is private. The public viewer has read-only
Firestore access, no Gemini secret, and no run endpoint.

10
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Both revisions serve one hundred percent of traffic.
The daily schedule and public security boundary are verified.

11
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Now the real production agent runs against the private worker.
Authentication is obtained internally and never printed.

12
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:50,000
This is one uninterrupted terminal recording.
The command is running against the deployed worker.

13
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Elapsed-time updates show that the same command is still running.
No token or private inventory payload is printed.

14
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:10,000
The result shows a Gemini forecast accepted as gemini_ok,
a Gemini briefing, and replay-safe dated inventory.

15
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Operational quantities still come from deterministic,
post-consumption ordering logic.

16
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:25,000
The refreshed dashboard traces the run from guest input,
through dish predictions, validation, FEFO, and publication.

17
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:36,000
The kitchen receives prioritized prep, today's shortage separately
from future orders, and supplier delivery dates.

18
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:46,000
The agent recommends how to resolve the shortage,
but clearly requires human approval.

19
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Gemini provides judgment.
Deterministic code owns the numbers.

20
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:03,000
The repository includes reproducible deployment instructions
and one hundred twenty-four passing tests.

21
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:09,000
Kitchen Prep Taskmaster runs the daily loop and shows its work.
Open the live read-only plan and inspect the evidence.
